###  https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000056
<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000056> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000053> ;
                                         rdfs:label "is orthorhombic"@de ;
                                         skos:definition "is orthorhombic is a object property  for the inference of family of directions/planes Miller indices notation under orthorhombic symmetry. The class crystallographic entity in orthorhombic system carries a Self restriction \"is orthorhombic\""@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000057
<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000057> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000053> ;
                                         rdfs:label "is rhombohedral"@de ;
                                         skos:definition "is rhombohedral is a object property  for the inference of family of directions/planes Miller indices notation under rhombohedral symmetry. The class crystallographic entity in rhombohedral system carries a Self restriction \"is rhombohedral\""@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000058
<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000058> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000053> ;
                                         rdfs:label "is hexagonal"@de ;
                                         skos:definition "is hexagonal is a object property  for the inference of family of directions/planes Miller indices notation under hexagonal symmetry. The class crystallographic entity in hexagonal system carries a Self restriction \"is hexagonal\""@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164
<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:comment "Intentially not a sub-property of \"denoted by\" as this rescticts using \"denoted by\" in property chains of its sub-properties" ,
                                                      "The sub-properties are inferrable through corresponding property chains" ;
                                         rdfs:label "denoted by family"@en ;
                                         skos:definition "denoted by family is a top-level object property between a crystallographic entity, i.e., plane or direction, and the family of Miller indices"@en ;
                                         skos:example "Consider a (011) crystallographic plane in cubic lattice, i.e., the instance of the plane is denoted by (011) instance. The instance of the plane is be inferred to be of type \"crystallographic entity in cubic system\" and carries \"is cubic\" reftexive triple. The (011) is a member of {110} family of Miller indices. The property chain \"is cubic + denoted by + member of\" will infer that the plane is denoted by {110} in a cubic lattice."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000168
<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000168> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> ;
                                         rdfs:label "denoted by family under cubic symmetry" ;
                                         skos:definition "denoted by family under cubic symmetry is an object property between a crystallographic entity in cubic system, i.e., plane or direction, and the family of Miller indices."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000170
<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000170> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000053> ;
                                         rdfs:label "is cubic" ;
                                         skos:definition "is cubic is a object property  for the inference of family of directions/planes Miller indices notation. The class crystallographic entity in cubic  system carries a Self restriction \"is cubic\""@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000066
noes:NOES_0000066 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:comment "This object property is not intended to be used between intances."@en ;
                  rdfs:label "geometrically related"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Geometrically related is a top-level object property to describe geometrical relations between different spatial regions"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000067
noes:NOES_0000067 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf noes:NOES_0000066 ;
                  rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ,
                           owl:TransitiveProperty ;
                  rdfs:label "parallel to"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Parallel to is an object property which connect two or  more spatial regions that are parallel to each other"@en ;
                  skos:example "normal direction (ND) of a rolled sheet is parallel to rolling plane RP."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000068
noes:NOES_0000068 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf noes:NOES_0000066 ;
                  rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                  owl:propertyChainAxiom ( noes:NOES_0000068
                                           noes:NOES_0000067
                                         ) ;
                  rdfs:label "normal to"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Normal to is a object property which describes geometric relation between two spatial regions which are normal to each other"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000131
noes:NOES_0000131 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf noes:NOES_0000066 ;
                  rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                  rdfs:label "approximately parallel to"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Approximately parallel to is an object property which connect two or  more spatial regions that are parallel to each other considering the misalignment angle of usually 15°"@en ;
                  skos:example "<111> family of directions in crystals are approximately parellel to normal direction (ND) of a sample in γ-fiber texture component"@en .


