###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000141
noes:NOES_0000141 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "misorentation angle"@en ;
                  skos:definition "misorientation angle is a relational quality that characterizes an angle between a crystallite in a microstructure and a reference crystallite with the ideal orientation of the specified crystallographic texture fiber or component. It is often used to determine if a crystallite contributes to this specific texture."@en ;
                  skos:example "9° misorientation between a crystallite with <hkl>{uvw} orientation and <100>{001} cube texture component."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000144
noes:NOES_0000144 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "crystallite with Goss texture orientation"@en ;
                  skos:comment "Note: this class is  not intended to be asserted, but inferred based on the grain orientation relative to the rolling reference frame. It is a part of the macroscopic texture inference."@en ;
                  skos:definition "crystallite with Goss texture orientation is a crystallite whose family of <001> equivalent directions in a cubic lattice system are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling direction and family of {110} equivalent directions are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling plane."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000151
noes:NOES_0000151 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "crystallite with rotated Goss texture orientation"@en ;
                  skos:comment "Note: this class is  not intended to be asserted, but inferred based on the grain orientation relative to the rolling reference frame. It is a part of the macroscopic texture inference."@en ;
                  skos:definition "crystallite with rotated Goss texture orientation is a crystallite whose family of <110> equivalent directions in a cubic lattice system are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling direction and family of {110} equivalent directions are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling plane."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000152
noes:NOES_0000152 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "crystallite with λ-fiber texture orientation"@en ;
                  skos:comment "Note: this class is  not intended to be asserted, but inferred based on the grain orientation relative to the rolling reference frame. It is a part of the macroscopic texture inference."@en ;
                  skos:definition "crystallite with  λ-fiber texture orientation is a crystallite whose family of <100> equivalent directions in a cubic lattice system are oriented approximately parallel to the normal direction."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000153
noes:NOES_0000153 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "diffraction process"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Diffraction process is a structural property analyzing process which utilizes diffraction of either electron, x-ray, or neutron waves to determine material's crystal structure, crystallographic texture, (phase) composition, and presence of defects."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000154
noes:NOES_0000154 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "diffractometer"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Diffractometer is a device which detects the intensity of a beam of either electrons, x-rays, or neutrons scattered from a material during a diffraction process."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000155
noes:NOES_0000155 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf noes:NOES_0000154 ;
                  rdfs:label "EBSD system"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Electron backscatter diffraction (EBSD) system is a diffractomter which detects diffracted electrons in the chamber of a scanning electron microscope."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000156
noes:NOES_0000156 rdf:type owl:Class ;
