                                  ] ;
                  rdfs:comment "The axiom is not expressible in OWL. SHACL restriction?"@en ;
                  rdfs:label "α*-fiber texture"@en ;
                  skos:altLabel "{h11}<1/h12>" ;
                  skos:definition "α*-fiber texture is a type of crystallographic texture which is quality of grain population, i.e., several grains, having a similar orientation (within a misorientation threshold) in relation to the material's reference frame: {11h} family of crystallographic planes are oriented parallel to the rolling plane of a sheet material and <1/h12> family of crystallographic directions are oriented parallel to the rolling direction (RD) of a sheet material."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000162
noes:NOES_0000162 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "crystallite with α-fiber texture orientation"@en ;
                  skos:comment "Note: this class is  not intended to be asserted, but inferred based on the grain orientation relative to the rolling reference frame. It is a part of the macroscopic texture inference."@en ;
                  skos:definition "crystallite with α-fiber texture orientation is a crystallite whose family of <110> equivalent directions in a cubic lattice system are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling direction."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000163
noes:NOES_0000163 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "magnetic properties measuring device"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Magnetic properties measuring device is a device that measures a hysteresis curve, i,e., its corresponding characteristic points, hysteresis loss, and total magnetic loss, of soft magnetic materials by applying alternating (AC) or quasi-static (DC) electric current on copper coils to produde external magnetic field."@en ;
                  skos:example "Single sheet tester (SST), Epstein frame, Ring core tester"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000164
noes:NOES_0000164 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "crystallite with α*-fiber texture orientation"@en ;
                  skos:comment "Note: this class is  not intended to be asserted, but inferred based on the grain orientation relative to the rolling reference frame. It is a part of the macroscopic texture inference."@en ,
                               "The axiom is not expressible in OWL. SHACL restriction?"@en ;
                  skos:definition "crystallite with α*-fiber texture orientation is a crystallite whose family of <1/h12> equivalent directions in a cubic lattice system are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling direction and family of {h11} equivalent directions are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling plane."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000165
noes:NOES_0000165 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "fillet radius"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Fillet radus is a charactereristic paramater of a geometry of a tensile test specimen which characterizes the radius of the curved sections (fillets) connecting the gripping ends to the reduced gauge length in a standard \"dog-bone\" specimen is specifically dimensioned to prevent stress concentrations from causing premature failure outside the gauge length."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000166
noes:NOES_0000166 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "average grain size"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Average grain size is an intensive quality of a material which describes the average diameter of grains in the material's microstructure."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000167
noes:NOES_0000167 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "crystallite with cube texture orientation"@en ;
                  skos:comment "Note: this class is  not intended to be asserted, but inferred based on the grain orientation relative to the rolling reference frame. It is a part of the macroscopic texture inference."@en ;
                  skos:definition "crystallite with cube texture orientation is a crystallite whose family of <100> equivalent directions in a cubic lattice system are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling direction and family of {001} equivalent directions are oriented approximately parallel to the rolling plane."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000168
noes:NOES_0000168 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "inverse pole figure" ;
                  skos:definition "An inverse pole figure is a stereographic projection that plots a specific, macroscopic physical direction of a sample, e.g., rolling or normal direction relative to the internal coordinate system of the crystal lattice, revealing the statistical frequency of grain orientations that align with that chosen physical axis."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000177
noes:NOES_0000177 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:label "grain population"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Grain population is a disconnected material aggregate which has crystallites ias parts.  Grain population represents grains which not necesserly spatially connected (unlike polycrystal) but share some collective quality, such as preffered crystallographic orientation."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000178
noes:NOES_0000178 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:comment """TODO add axioms
1. When the magnetic qualities are realized
2. Especially for peak values that would be interesting"""@en ;
                  rdfs:label "magnetic polarization"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Magnetic polarization is a magnetic property which is a measure of intrinsic magnetization of a material (alignment of magnetic dipoles) as a response to the externaly applied magnetic field H. It is determined as a difference between magnetic induction B and the external field µ0*H."@en ;
                  co:symbol "J" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000179
noes:NOES_0000179 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:comment """deprecated axiom: 'has part' some 
(microstructure and ('has quality' some 
(PMD_0025003 and ('specified by value' value ferrite))))""" ;
                  rdfs:label "electrical steel"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Electrical steel is a steel material which has only ferritic metallic grain structure and uses silicon as the main alloying element. It manufactured in a form of a sheet and designed to exibit superior magenetic properties either in all directions (non-orieneted) or in a sinlge direction (oriented)."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000180
noes:NOES_0000180 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf noes:NOES_0000179 ;
                  rdfs:label "non-oriented electrical steel"@en ;
                  skos:altLabel "NOES" ;
                  skos:definition "Non-oriented electrical steel is an electrical steel material which exhibits isotropic magnetic properties in all direction in the sheet plane."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000181
noes:NOES_0000181 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf noes:NOES_0000180 ;
                  rdfs:comment """TODO: 
1. Import W/kg units
2. Add units to the equivalent class
3. Think of adding nomical thickness class
4. Check the some in the decimal"""@en ;
                  rdfs:label "NO27-14"@en ;
                  skos:definition "NO27-14 is a non-oriented electrical steel which has characteristic total magnetic losses P1.0/400 of max 14 W/kg and a quality thickness of 0.27 mm."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000182
noes:NOES_0000182 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf noes:NOES_0000178 ;
                  rdfs:label "peak magnetic polarization"@en ;
                  skos:altLabel "saturation polatization"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Peak magnetic polarization is a maximum magnetic polarization that a material exhibits under the applied external magnetic field Hmax."@en ;
                  co:symbol "Jsat"@en ,
                            "Jmax" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000183
noes:NOES_0000183 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf noes:NOES_0000163 ;
                  obo:IAO_0000119 "https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epsteinrahmen" ;
                  rdfs:label "Epstein frame"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Epstein frame is a measuring device of magnetic properties of soft magnetic materials, especially electrical steels. It consists of outer primary (magnetizing) winding, which surrounds the inner secondary (measuring) winding, and both windings are distributed across the four coils of the  frame. The steel strips are inserted pairwise into the opposite coils."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000184
noes:NOES_0000184 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf noes:NOES_0000163 ;
                  obo:IAO_0000119 "https://www.magnet-physik.de/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/MJC-210-e-3236.pdf" ;
                  rdfs:label "sinlge sheet tester"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Single sheet tester is a measuring device of soft magnetic properties of sheet materials, especially electrical steels. It consists of a single coil system to magnetize the sample with and and a pick-up coil to detect  polarization in the material."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/noes/NOES_0000185
noes:NOES_0000185 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf noes:NOES_0000163 ;
                  obo:IAO_0000119 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rowland_ring" ;
                  rdfs:label "thoroidal core setup"@en ;
                  skos:altLabel "ring core setup"@en ;
                  skos:definition "Thoroidal core setup is a measuring device of a hysteresis curve of magnetic materials. The specimen shape is a thoroid, around which a magnitization coil is closely wound."@en .


